// The words the factory's parts pass to each other. One file, because an
// enum can only name types declared in its own file (finding 29).
//
// DRAFT 1 (2026-11-28). Nothing here is built yet; CHOICE TO CONFIRM (F1,
// F2, ...) marks what the user has not decided.

// ---- What goes in and comes out.

// A Mitra model: the project's .mitra files. The factory states nothing of
// what is inside; Mitra reads it.
subject record Model { .. }
// The code: the project's files other than the model (sources, tests,
// build files). Opaque, like the model.
subject record Tree { .. }
// What changed between two versions of a model: parts, claims, ensures,
// rows added, removed or changed. QUESTION Q5: who computes it.
subject record ModelDiff { .. }

// ---- What Mitra says (its four verdicts, counted over the model's ensures).

subject record Tally { explained: integer, assumed: integer, contradicted: integer, unsupported: integer }
// Mitra's reasons when `check` refuses a model, and the weakest links when
// `blame` runs. Text the coding harness reads in the next brief.
subject record Diagnostics { .. }

// ---- What the tests say.

// CHOICE TO CONFIRM (F1): the test capabilities a project may switch on.
subject enum Capability { Unit, Property, Coverage, Mutation }
// One run of the capabilities switched on: how many checks failed. A
// coverage or mutation score under its setting counts as one failure.
subject record TestReport { failed: integer }

// ---- What the coding harness is told, and what it can fail with.

// CHOICE TO CONFIRM (F2): the harnesses known to the factory. Fake is the
// POC's: scripted by tests, like the assistant's fake models.
subject enum CoderKind { Fake, ClaudeCode, OpenCode }
// What the harness is asked to do in one round: the model, the diff when
// there is one, and what the last round got wrong. Text; opaque here.
subject record Brief { .. }
subject enum CoderFailure { Unreachable, Crashed, OutOfBudget }

// ---- How a run ends.

subject enum Stop {
    Done,            // every promise met, every test passes
    OutOfRounds,     // the rounds set were used up
    ModelRefused,    // Mitra's check refused the model: no code was written
    CoderFailed      // the coding harness could not work (F4)
}
// What the factory hands back: the code as it is, Mitra's tally of it, how
// the run ended and in how many rounds.
subject record Delivery { tree: Tree, tally: Tally, stop: Stop, rounds: integer }
